{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":393252,"num_turns":26,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7dd2c99a-16df-4154-8b7c-06354780f87e","total_cost_usd":2.4136279999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91839,"cache_read_input_tokens":1431536,"output_tokens":31172,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91839,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":106409,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":31172,"cacheReadInputTokens":1431536,"cacheCreationInputTokens":91839,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.4136279999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**`work-loop-v2-intake-router`, Unit 1 — discovery done, no premise failed, handed back to Codex** (commit `c2036d5`, state file only).\n\nAll eight brief claims hold on inspection. Two were true but needed a boundary correction, and one predicted staleness that turned out real:\n\n- **The command count is 94, not 88.** `ai-resources/.claude/commands/` has 88, but a second surface at workspace root adds 6 more real files on top of 57 symlinks.\n- **The six design/motion skills are Codex-only** — none is installed on the Claude side, so excluding them costs the Claude side nothing.\n- **The README is genuinely stale**, as the brief predicted: it says `diagnosing-bugs` is missing, but it is installed now, and its list is 14 names short of the live 25.\n\n**The finding that matters.** The two skill surfaces are not symmetric. Of the 25 Matt skills, **12 exist only on the Claude side** — including `ask-matt` itself, which is also marked never-auto-invoke. So a router living on the Codex side cannot link to `ask-matt`, and cannot reach almost half the destinations `ask-matt` maps. The flow `ask-matt` describes starts at `grill-with-docs` and both its on-ramps (`triage`, `diagnosing-bugs`) are Claude-only.\n\n**Recommended shape:** a compact index of Class 1 only — 16 Axcíon commands plus 12 Matt skills, 28 entries, trigger conditions and names, no procedures — inside the Routing section that `.agents/skills/work-loop-v2/SKILL.md` already has. Not a new file, not a catalogue.\n\n**Three things I did not guess and left for you:**\n1. `/triage`, `/handoff` and `/grill-me` each mean two different things — an Axcíon command and a Matt skill. `/triage` is the worst: reviewing Claude's own proposals vs. working an issue tracker. Nothing overlaps.\n2. Should a Codex-side router advertise the 12 Claude-only skills, marked as such, or leave them out?\n3. Six workspace-root-only commands (`harness-start`, `session-report`, `resolve-improvements`, `run-qc`, `update-md`, `validate`) appear in none of the brief's lists — still in use?\n\nChoices 1 and 2 both change what the index names, so Unit 2 cannot be briefed as Implementation until they are settled.\n\nOne scope correction mid-unit: I first wrote the evidence as a script under `logs/scripts/`, then removed it — the brief allows changing the state file only. The check runs from the shell instead, and its failing case was built first in both directions (deleting a Claude name and a Codex name each make it exit 1).\n\nAssessment is Codex's move.","ttft_ms":3079,"ttft_stream_ms":2431,"time_to_request_ms":32,"type":"result","duration_ms":398230,"uuid":"1779de13-be60-46fc-b5be-ef1d039e97ae"}
